      "message": "I can\u0027t find a single thing in the data sheet about when LRESET would fire. Looking at just how the code is written this handler expects both edges (rising and falling) of LRESET#. However, the bug is that the interrupt fires, but the bus monitor is showing something else? How is that possible? Are we seeing a runt rise followed by a decay than a re-rise?\n\nAlso, why aren\u0027t we just signaling to a task to take care of LPC events? We just needed to know that one happened, right? Couldn\u0027t we do the filtering in that task?",
